termediate"><addressbook><name>IHASHI, TAKAO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>INOKUCHI, TATSUYA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OGAWA, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAKO, YOICHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO, MASANOBU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An optical disk comprises a substrate, on one side of which a first recording layer and a second recording layer of different reflectivities are formed one on another, and a protective coating is provided on the first or second recording layer, which is farther from the substrate. For reproduction, a light beam is emitted from a single light source to the first or second recording layer through a single object lens. Based on whether the light beam is reflected from the first or second recording layer, the object lens is moved along its optical axis and focused on the recording layer to reproduce information.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un disque optique qui comprend un substrat, sur un côté duquel sont formées des première et seconde couches d'enregistrement superposées n'ayant pas la même réflectivité. Le disque optique comprend en outre un revêtement protecteur sur la première ou seconde couche d'enregistrement, à une distance plus grande par rapport au substrat. Aux fins de reproduction, un faisceau lumineux est émis par une source lumineuse unique, en direction de la première ou seconde couche d'enregistrement, via une lentille objet unique. Selon que ledit faisceau est réfléchi par la première ou seconde couche d'enregistrement, la lentille objet est déplacée le long de son axe optique et focalisée sur la couche d'enregistrement aux fins de reproduction de l'information.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>